    {
      "type": "teaser",
      "visible": true,
      "title": "",
      "content": {
        "media": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "assets/img-000.jpg",
            "caption": "GARD restores degraded multi-view inputs jointly in geometry-aware feature space, recovering accurate 3D point clouds and high-quality RGB images simultaneously.",
            "alt": "Figure 1 — GARD framework: degraded views and depths (left) are transformed into restored views, depths, and a clean 3D point cloud (right)."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "bacc49bd"
    },
    {
      "type": "tldr",
      "visible": true,
      "title": "TL;DR",
      "content": {
        "text": "**~#a51fb7:GARD~** performs diffusion-based denoising directly in the **~#a51fb7:geometry-aware feature space~** of a feed-forward 3D reconstructor — not in pixel space or compressed VAE latents — enabling simultaneous recovery of accurate 3D geometry and high-quality multi-view imagery from degraded inputs."
      },
      "id": "30d2c5fe"
    },
    {
      "id": "2062a193",
      "type": "image",
      "visible": true,
      "content": {
        "media": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "assets/img-001.jpg",
            "caption": "",
            "alt": ""
          }
        ]
      },
      "title": "Pixel-Space and VAE-Based Restoration Fall Short for 3D Reconstruction",
      "sectionLabel": "MOTIVATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "visible": true,
      "content": {
        "text": "Feed-forward 3D reconstruction models perform well under clean conditions, but fail under real-world degradations such as motion blur.\n\n\n**~#a51fb7:Where should restoration happen?~**\n\n⚠️ Pixel-space restoration: Ignores cross-view consistency \n\n⚠️ Multi-view restoration in VAE-based latent space: Loses fine-grained spatial details\n\n 💡 **GARD**: Restores directly in the **geometry-aware feature space**  \n\n**~#a51fb7:Key Insight~**: The reconstructor’s intermediate feature space preserves both cross-view consistency and visual detail, making it more suitable for restoration than pixel space or compressed VAE latents.",
        "bulletItems": []
      },
      "id": "abd4bf96"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "visible": true,
      "sectionLabel": "METHOD",
      "title": "Overall Framework",
      "content": {
        "media": [
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "assets/img-002.jpg",
            "caption": "The GARD denoiser is inserted at layer K of a frozen multi-view encoder, restoring degraded representations before they propagate to geometry and RGB decoders.",
            "alt": "Figure 3 — GARD framework overview: (a) denoiser inserted into frozen multi-view encoder, (b) training with interpolated flow matching + attention alignment loss, (c) multi-view DDT encoder-decoder architecture with global and frame attention layers."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "4f35cc8c",
      "paddingBottom": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "9e8dddcd",
      "type": "text",
      "visible": true,
      "content": {
        "text": "",
        "bulletItems": [
          "**~#a51fb7:Encode Features~**: Degraded multi-view images are encoded by a frozen multi-view encoder to produce layer-wise latent representations.",
          "**~#a51fb7:Representation Denoising~**: The GARD denoiser restores these degraded features using a multi-view diffusion model with interleaved frame-level and global cross-view attention.",
          "**~#a51fb7:Task-Specific Decoding~**: The restored representations are decoded by their respective decoders to produce geometry predictions and restored RGB images."
        ]
      }
    },
